.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH specport 1 2026-11-20 "sandogasa 0.29.0" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
specport \- Port RPM specs between build systems, starting with autotools to Meson
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBspecport\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Port RPM specs between build systems, starting with autotools to Meson
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS specport autotools-to-meson
\fBspecport autotools\-to\-meson\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-source\fR> <\fISPEC\fR>
.PP
Convert a spec\*(Aqs %configure and make steps to Meson\*(Aqs, mapping its configure options to the new source\*(Aqs Meson options
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color the diff: auto (on a terminal), always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Auto\-detect: enable on a TTY when `NO_COLOR` is unset
.IP \(bu 2
always: Force colored output even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Disable colored output entirely
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the converted spec and the notes as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
The new source: its unpacked tree, or its tarball
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
Write the converted spec in place, keeping the original as <spec>.orig, rather than showing a diff
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISPEC\fR>
The spec to convert
